// Electric fence -- a FENCE WiFi GATEWAY GW100 and two PDX70 energizers.
//
// Unlike ATMOS this is not read over the LAN. The gateway has no local
// service at all: 1039 TCP ports closed, no UDP, no mDNS. It holds one
// outbound connection to fencee Cloud and every reading and command goes
// through there. So the binding signs in with the phone app's account and
// addresses devices by their cloud id -- no IP, nothing DHCP can break.
//
// That has one consequence for rules and for the sitemap: when the internet
// or the cloud is down the binding sees nothing. It sets the channels to
// UNDEF rather than leaving the last reading in place, because a stale
// voltage would look exactly like a live fence. last-update is the one
// channel it leaves alone, so staleness stays renderable.
//
// Copy to fenceecloud.things and fill in. That file is gitignored because it
// carries the account password. The ids are placeholders too: mihyb/smart-home
// is a public repository and the gateway id is the pairing identifier fencee's
// cloud knows it by. The real values are in captured/gateways.json in the
// fencee-connector submodule, which is private.
//
// Config keys come from org.openhab.binding.fenceecloud (the fencee-connector
// submodule). clientId is left at its default on purpose: it registers this
// binding in the account's own device list, so a changing value would add a
// row there on every restart.
//
// The Things are nested inside the account Bridge on purpose. openHAB derives
// a nested Thing's UID from its bridge, so nesting is what produces
// fenceecloud:energizer:home:upper -- the same shape discovery would create.
// Declared standalone with a (bridge) reference they would come out as
// fenceecloud:energizer:upper instead, and every item link would resolve to
// nothing while the Thing still showed ONLINE. That failure has happened here
// before with mqtt:topic:bojler_switch, in the opposite direction.
//
// Discovery also finds both energizers from the account alone, but it names
// them by device id. Do not accept them from the inbox as well -- they would
// be second Things with different UIDs, and the item links point here.

Bridge fenceecloud:account:home "fencee Cloud" [
    email="<<SET_ME>>",
    password="<<SET_ME>>",
    refreshInterval=300
] {
    Thing gateway gw "Ohradník brána" [
        gatewayId="<<SET_ME>>"
    ]

    Thing energizer upper "Ohradník horní" [
        deviceId="<<SET_ME>>",
        gatewayId="<<SET_ME>>"
    ]

    Thing energizer lower "Ohradník spodní" [
        deviceId="<<SET_ME>>",
        gatewayId="<<SET_ME>>"
    ]
}
